            "review_title": "Review at LABRI - Oriental Neo Bistro",
            "review_text": "Andy\nTaipei, Taiwan388 contributions\n0\nFusion Hits and Misses\nJul 2025 • Solo\nLABRI’s modern fusion menu had hits and misses. The amaebi cold pasta impressed me with its dessert-like texture: smooth, creamy, and sweet. The red sea bream was equally strong. Its riso pasta absorbed sake beurre blanc and clam dashi for an umami-rich bite. However, the consistency faltered on the main course. The Australian wagyu flap was disappointing due to amateurish plating. An oversized garnish dominated the plate, and its monochromatic look lacked vibrancy. While the server was attentive, his explanations of each course were too quiet to hear. A promising spot for fusion fans, but still in need of polish and consistency.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nSkip the truffle add-on for the main. At ~500k VND for 2g, it felt pricey for the flavor boost. Ask about truffle type to ensure value.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten August 14, 2025",
            "rating": 3.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
